Interpretation (no fabrication):

- VERIFIED (setup path): `supabase start` -> `supabase db reset` applies all 75 migrations AND
  seeds from `[db.seed].sql_paths` in supabase/config.toml (all 6 seed files observed). The seeded
  user `marcus@seed.test` exists in the local DB, and the generated `test-signin.json` matches it,
  so the committed-credential dependency is genuinely closed.
- BLOCKED at this first run (test execution): every auth.spec test failed at browser *launch*,
  because the ci-runner LXC lacked `libglib-2.0.so.0`. See section 11 for the re-run after the OS
  libraries were installed.
- Workflow hardened: `pnpm exec playwright install --with-deps chromium` so CI installs the
  Chromium OS libraries the lab lacked.
- Historical note: the first E2E attempt (at commit 0432329) discovered that `supabase db execute`
  is not a valid subcommand in Supabase CLI 2.119.0 and that the original separate seed step was
  both wrong and redundant; the final commit relies on `supabase db reset` seeding and drops the
  extra step. That bug was found only because this E2E run was executed.

